IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa14-nouns`
IMPORT `coa14-ch08-alteration`

-- coa14-ch10-reduction.l4: Companies Act 2006, Part 17 Chapter 10 "Reduction of share capital", ss 641 to 653 (lines 8527-8709).
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively, from the text alone. How to read an answer: see coa14-ch07-premiums.l4 (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE with
-- a FALSE-kind comment, NOTHING with a NOTHING-kind comment). A function titled as a bar answers JUST TRUE where the text says no
-- to the act, JUST FALSE where the bar does not apply, NOTHING where the text does not decide.
-- This module imports coa14-ch08-alteration.l4 for the one statement-of-capital rule (`s 619(3) the statement of capital states
-- what the section requires`) that ss 644(2) and 649(2) repeat.
-- SEAMS: facts another part answers are inputs named for the answering section (s 283, s 1121, s 4(1), s 3(2), s 988, s 1062 ...).

§ `Chapter 10 -- Reduction of share capital`

§§ `s 641 Circumstances in which a company may reduce its share capital`

-- src:8530 | (1) A limited company having a share capital may reduce its share capital—
-- src:8531 | (a) in the case of a private company limited by shares, by special resolution supported by a solvency statement (see sections 642 to 644);
-- src:8532 | (b) in any case, by special resolution confirmed by the court (see sections 645 to 651).
@ref s 641(1) Circumstances in which a company may reduce its share capital: the routes (src:8530-8532)
GIVEN `the company is a limited company having a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      route IS A `s 641(1) route of reduction`
      `s 4(1) the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 3(2) the company is limited by shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 283 the resolution is a special resolution` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 642(1) the resolution is supported by a solvency statement` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the resolution is confirmed by the court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 641(1) the company may reduce its share capital by this route` MEANS
    IF NOT `the company is a limited company having a share capital`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is that of "A limited company having a share capital"
    ELSE CONSIDER route
         WHEN `s 641(1)(a) special resolution supported by a solvency statement` THEN
             IF NOT (`s 4(1) the company is a private company` AND `s 3(2) the company is limited by shares`)
             THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): (a) is "in the case of a private company limited by shares"
             ELSE IF `s 283 the resolution is a special resolution` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `s 642(1) the resolution is supported by a solvency statement` EQUALS JUST TRUE
                  THEN JUST TRUE
                  ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant is for a reduction "by special resolution supported by a solvency statement"; without both the text does not say (fork F-grant-limit)
         WHEN `s 641(1)(b) special resolution confirmed by the court` THEN
             IF `s 283 the resolution is a special resolution` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the resolution is confirmed by the court`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant is for a reduction "by special resolution confirmed by the court"; without both the text does not say (fork F-grant-limit)

-- src:8533 | (2) A company may not reduce its capital under subsection (1)(a) if as a result of the reduction there would no longer be any member of the company holding shares other than redeemable shares.
@ref s 641(2) Circumstances in which a company may reduce its share capital: no member left holding other than redeemable shares (src:8533)
GIVEN route IS A `s 641(1) route of reduction`
      `after the reduction no member of the company would hold shares other than redeemable shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 641(2) the section bars the reduction under subsection (1)(a)` MEANS
    CONSIDER route
    WHEN `s 641(1)(b) special resolution confirmed by the court` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is on a reduction "under subsection (1)(a)"
    WHEN `s 641(1)(a) special resolution supported by a solvency statement` THEN
        IF `after the reduction no member of the company would hold shares other than redeemable shares`
        THEN JUST TRUE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company may not reduce its capital under subsection (1)(a) if as a result of the reduction there would no longer be any member of the company holding shares other than redeemable shares"
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may not reduce its capital under subsection (1)(a) if ..." (the "if" is not met: marginal reading (a))

-- (2C) "scheme" means a compromise or arrangement sanctioned by the court under Part 26 or 26A; "associate" has the meaning
-- given by s 988, reading references to an offeror as references to the person acquiring the shares in the company.
-- src:8541 | “scheme” means a compromise or arrangement sanctioned by the court under Part 26 or 26A (arrangements and reconstructions).
@ref s 641(2C) Circumstances in which a company may reduce its share capital: "scheme" (src:8541)
GIVEN `it is a compromise or arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is sanctioned by the court under Part 26 or 26A` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 641(2C) the arrangement is a scheme` MEANS
    IF `it is a compromise or arrangement` AND `it is sanctioned by the court under Part 26 or 26A`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“scheme” means a compromise or arrangement sanctioned by the court under Part 26 or 26A"

-- src:8540 | “associate” has the meaning given by section 988 (meaning of “associate”), reading references in that section to an offeror as references to the person acquiring the shares in the company;
@ref s 641(2C) Circumstances in which a company may reduce its share capital: "associate" (src:8540)
GIVEN `s 988 the person is an associate of the person acquiring the shares in the company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 641(2C) the person is an associate` MEANS
    `s 988 the person is an associate of the person acquiring the shares in the company` -- the meaning is s 988's (coa21), reading an offeror as the person acquiring the shares: JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING as that section answers

-- src:8535 | (2B) Subsection (2A) does not apply to a scheme under which—
-- src:8536 | (a) the company is to have a new parent undertaking,
-- src:8537 | (b) all or substantially all of the members of the company become members of the parent undertaking, and
-- src:8538 | (c) the members of the company are to hold proportions of the equity share capital of the parent undertaking in the same or substantially the same proportions as they hold the equity share capital of the company.
@ref s 641(2B) Circumstances in which a company may reduce its share capital: the carve-out (src:8535-8538)
GIVEN `the company is to have a new parent undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all or substantially all of the members of the company become members of the parent undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the members hold proportions of the equity share capital of the parent undertaking in the same or substantially the same proportions as they hold the equity share capital of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 641(2B) subsection (2A) does not apply to the scheme` MEANS
    IF       `the company is to have a new parent undertaking`
         AND `all or substantially all of the members of the company become members of the parent undertaking`
         AND `the members hold proportions of the equity share capital of the parent undertaking in the same or substantially the same proportions as they hold the equity share capital of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the carve-out names only a scheme under which (a), (b) and (c) all hold; for any other scheme it says nothing

-- src:8534 | (2A) A company may not reduce its share capital under subsection (1)(a) or (b) as part of a scheme by virtue of which a person, or a person together with its associates, is to acquire all the shares in the company or (where there is more than one class of shares in a company) all the shares of one or more classes, in each case other than shares that are already held by that person or its associates.
@ref s 641(2A) Circumstances in which a company may reduce its share capital: reduction as part of a takeover scheme (src:8534)
GIVEN `s 641(2C) the arrangement is a scheme` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `by virtue of the scheme a person, or a person together with its associates, is to acquire all the shares in the company other than shares already held by that person or its associates` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has more than one class of shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `by virtue of the scheme a person, or a person together with its associates, is to acquire all the shares of one or more classes other than shares already held by that person or its associates` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 641(2B) subsection (2A) does not apply to the scheme` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 641(2A) the section bars the reduction as part of the scheme` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 641(2C) the arrangement is a scheme` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the bar is on a reduction "as part of a scheme"; "scheme" means a compromise or arrangement sanctioned under Part 26 or 26A (fork F-act-description)
        IF NOT (   `by virtue of the scheme a person, or a person together with its associates, is to acquire all the shares in the company other than shares already held by that person or its associates`
                OR (`the company has more than one class of shares` AND `by virtue of the scheme a person, or a person together with its associates, is to acquire all the shares of one or more classes other than shares already held by that person or its associates`))
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the bar is on a scheme "by virtue of which a person, or a person together with its associates, is to acquire all the shares in the company or ... all the shares of one or more classes" (fork F-act-description)
        IF `s 641(2B) subsection (2A) does not apply to the scheme` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (2A) does not apply to a scheme under which"
        IF `s 641(2C) the arrangement is a scheme` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the arrangement was sanctioned by the court under Part 26 or 26A is not known
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company may not reduce its share capital under subsection (1)(a) or (b) as part of a scheme by virtue of which a person ... is to acquire all the shares"

-- Subsection (2) bars only a reduction "under subsection (1)(a)": for route (b) it is not an obstacle, so it is read as a bar that does not apply.
-- src:8542 | (3) Subject to subsections (2) to (2B), a company may reduce its share capital under this section in any way.
@ref s 641(3) Circumstances in which a company may reduce its share capital: in any way (src:8542)
GIVEN route IS A `s 641(1) route of reduction`
      `s 641(2) the section bars the reduction under subsection (1)(a)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 641(2A) the section bars the reduction as part of the scheme` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 641(3) the company may reduce its share capital in the way proposed` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF bar2 EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `s 641(2A) the section bars the reduction as part of the scheme` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to subsections (2) to (2B), a company may reduce its share capital under this section in any way" (a subsection bars the reduction)
        IF bar2 EQUALS JUST FALSE AND `s 641(2A) the section bars the reduction as part of the scheme` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subject to subsections (2) to (2B)": a bar whose answer is not known leaves "in any way" unanswered
    WHERE
        bar2 MEANS
            CONSIDER route
            WHEN `s 641(1)(b) special resolution confirmed by the court` THEN JUST FALSE -- subsection (2) is a bar on a reduction "under subsection (1)(a)" only
            WHEN `s 641(1)(a) special resolution supported by a solvency statement` THEN `s 641(2) the section bars the reduction under subsection (1)(a)`

-- src:8543 | (4) In particular, a company may—
-- src:8544 | (a) extinguish or reduce the liability on any of its shares in respect of share capital not paid up, or
-- src:8545 | (b) either with or without extinguishing or reducing liability on any of its shares—
-- src:8546 | (i) cancel any paid-up share capital that is lost or unrepresented by available assets, or
-- src:8547 | (ii) repay any paid-up share capital in excess of the company's wants.
@ref s 641(4) Circumstances in which a company may reduce its share capital: in particular (src:8543-8547)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 641(4) kind of reduction`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 641(4) the reduction is of a kind the section names` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 641(4)(a) extinguishing or reducing the liability on shares in respect of share capital not paid up` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 641(4)(b)(i) cancelling paid-up share capital that is lost or unrepresented by available assets` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 641(4)(b)(ii) repaying paid-up share capital in excess of the company's wants` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 641(4) some other kind of reduction` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "In particular, a company may" does not close the list, and subsection (3) already allows "any way"

-- src:8548 | (5) A special resolution under this section may not provide for a reduction of share capital to take effect later than the date on which the resolution has effect in accordance with this Chapter.
@ref s 641(5) Circumstances in which a company may reduce its share capital: no later effect (src:8548)
GIVEN `the date the resolution provides for the reduction to take effect` IS A DATE
      `the date the resolution has effect in accordance with this Chapter` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 641(5) the resolution is barred from providing for that date` MEANS
    IF `the date the resolution provides for the reduction to take effect` GREATER THAN `the date the resolution has effect in accordance with this Chapter`
    THEN JUST TRUE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A special resolution under this section may not provide for a reduction of share capital to take effect later than the date on which the resolution has effect in accordance with this Chapter"
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may not provide for a reduction ... to take effect later than" (the date is not later)

-- src:8549 | (6) This Chapter (apart from subsection (5) above) has effect subject to any provision of the company's articles restricting or prohibiting the reduction of the company's share capital.
@ref s 641(6) Circumstances in which a company may reduce its share capital: the articles (src:8549)
GIVEN `the articles contain a provision restricting or prohibiting the reduction of the company's share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reduction is one that provision restricts or prohibits` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 641(6) the company's articles bar the reduction` MEANS
    IF `the articles contain a provision restricting or prohibiting the reduction of the company's share capital` AND `the reduction is one that provision restricts or prohibits`
    THEN JUST TRUE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This Chapter (apart from subsection (5) above) has effect subject to any provision of the company's articles restricting or prohibiting the reduction of the company's share capital"
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "subject to any provision of the company's articles restricting or prohibiting the reduction" (these articles do not: fork F-articles)

-- src:8550 | (7) In subsection (1)(b), section 91(5)(b)(iii), sections 645 to 651 (except in the phrases “sanctioned by the court under Part 26” and “sanctioned by the court under Part 26A”) and 653(1) “the court” means, in England and Wales, the High Court.
@ref s 641(7) Circumstances in which a company may reduce its share capital: "the court" (src:8550)
GIVEN `the place where the company is registered` IS A `Place of registration`
      `the reference is in the phrase "sanctioned by the court under Part 26" or "sanctioned by the court under Part 26A"` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 641(7) the court is the High Court` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the place where the company is registered`
    WHEN `England and Wales` THEN
        IF `the reference is in the phrase "sanctioned by the court under Part 26" or "sanctioned by the court under Part 26A"`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(except in the phrases “sanctioned by the court under Part 26” and “sanctioned by the court under Part 26A”)"
        ELSE JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Scotland` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the text speaks only of England and Wales; the court elsewhere is s 1156 (coa25)
    WHEN `Northern Ireland` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the text speaks only of England and Wales; the court elsewhere is s 1156 (coa25)

-- E1 option B, gathered by hand: the route of (1) with (2) to (2B) and (3).
-- src:8530 | (1) A limited company having a share capital may reduce its share capital—
-- src:8531 | (a) in the case of a private company limited by shares, by special resolution supported by a solvency statement (see sections 642 to 644);
-- src:8532 | (b) in any case, by special resolution confirmed by the court (see sections 645 to 651).
-- src:8533 | (2) A company may not reduce its capital under subsection (1)(a) if as a result of the reduction there would no longer be any member of the company holding shares other than redeemable shares.
-- src:8534 | (2A) A company may not reduce its share capital under subsection (1)(a) or (b) as part of a scheme by virtue of which a person, or a person together with its associates, is to acquire all the shares in the company or (where there is more than one class of shares in a company) all the shares of one or more classes, in each case other than shares that are already held by that person or its associates.
-- src:8535 | (2B) Subsection (2A) does not apply to a scheme under which—
-- src:8536 | (a) the company is to have a new parent undertaking,
-- src:8537 | (b) all or substantially all of the members of the company become members of the parent undertaking, and
-- src:8538 | (c) the members of the company are to hold proportions of the equity share capital of the parent undertaking in the same or substantially the same proportions as they hold the equity share capital of the company.
-- src:8539 | (2C) In this section—
-- src:8540 | “associate” has the meaning given by section 988 (meaning of “associate”), reading references in that section to an offeror as references to the person acquiring the shares in the company;
-- src:8541 | “scheme” means a compromise or arrangement sanctioned by the court under Part 26 or 26A (arrangements and reconstructions).
-- src:8542 | (3) Subject to subsections (2) to (2B), a company may reduce its share capital under this section in any way.
@ref s 641 the company may reduce its share capital by the route, subject to subsections (2) to (2B) (src:8530-8542)
GIVEN `s 641(1) the company may reduce its share capital by this route` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 641(3) the company may reduce its share capital in the way proposed` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 641(6) the company's articles bar the reduction` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 641 the reduction of share capital is within the section` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 641(3) the company may reduce its share capital in the way proposed` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to subsections (2) to (2B)"
        IF `s 641(6) the company's articles bar the reduction` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "has effect subject to any provision of the company's articles restricting or prohibiting the reduction"
        IF       `s 641(1) the company may reduce its share capital by this route` EQUALS JUST TRUE
             AND `s 641(3) the company may reduce its share capital in the way proposed` EQUALS JUST TRUE
             AND `s 641(6) the company's articles bar the reduction` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): not every limb of the section is answered

§§ `s 642 Reduction of capital supported by solvency statement`

-- (a) the statement is made "not more than 15 days before the date on which the resolution is passed": made on a day from 15 days
-- before the resolution to the day of the resolution. A statement dated AFTER the resolution is not "before" it: NOTHING (fork).
-- src:8553 | (1) A resolution for reducing share capital of a private company limited by shares is supported by a solvency statement if—
-- src:8554 | (a) the directors of the company make a statement of the solvency of the company in accordance with section 643 (a “solvency statement”) not more than 15 days before the date on which the resolution is passed, and
-- src:8555 | (b) the resolution and solvency statement are registered in accordance with section 644.
@ref s 642(1) Reduction of capital supported by solvency statement (src:8553-8555)
GIVEN `the company is a private company limited by shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the directors made the statement` IS A DATE
      `the date the resolution is passed` IS A DATE
      `s 643 the statement is made in accordance with section 643` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the resolution and the solvency statement are registered in accordance with section 644` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 642(1) the resolution is supported by a solvency statement` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the company is a private company limited by shares`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the definition is of "A resolution for reducing share capital of a private company limited by shares"
        IF `the date the directors made the statement` GREATER THAN `the date the resolution is passed`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the statement must be made "before" the resolution; the text does not say what a later statement is
        IF `the date the directors made the statement` LESS THAN (`the date the resolution is passed` MINUS 15)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is supported by a solvency statement if— (a) the directors ... make a statement of the solvency of the company ... not more than 15 days before the date on which the resolution is passed"
        IF `s 643 the statement is made in accordance with section 643` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) the directors of the company make a statement of the solvency of the company in accordance with section 643"
        IF NOT `the resolution and the solvency statement are registered in accordance with section 644`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is supported by a solvency statement if— ... (b) the resolution and solvency statement are registered in accordance with section 644"
        IF `s 643 the statement is made in accordance with section 643` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the statement was made in accordance with s 643 is not known
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:8556 | (2) Where the resolution is proposed as a written resolution, a copy of the solvency statement must be sent or submitted to every eligible member at or before the time at which the proposed resolution is sent or submitted to him.
@ref s 642(2) Reduction of capital supported by solvency statement: written resolution (src:8556)
GIVEN `the resolution is proposed as a written resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a copy of the solvency statement was sent or submitted to the eligible member at or before the time at which the proposed resolution was sent or submitted to him` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 642(2) the copy of the solvency statement was sent or submitted to the eligible member in time` MEANS
    IF NOT `the resolution is proposed as a written resolution`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where the resolution is proposed as a written resolution" (fork F-where-unmet)
    ELSE IF `a copy of the solvency statement was sent or submitted to the eligible member at or before the time at which the proposed resolution was sent or submitted to him`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a copy of the solvency statement must be sent or submitted to every eligible member at or before the time at which the proposed resolution is sent or submitted to him" (a bare "must" not done: fork F-must)

-- src:8557 | (3) Where the resolution is proposed at a general meeting, a copy of the solvency statement must be made available for inspection by members of the company throughout that meeting.
@ref s 642(3) Reduction of capital supported by solvency statement: general meeting (src:8557)
GIVEN `the resolution is proposed at a general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a copy of the solvency statement was made available for inspection by members of the company throughout that meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 642(3) the copy of the solvency statement was made available for inspection throughout the meeting` MEANS
    IF NOT `the resolution is proposed at a general meeting`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where the resolution is proposed at a general meeting" (fork F-where-unmet)
    ELSE IF `a copy of the solvency statement was made available for inspection by members of the company throughout that meeting`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a copy of the solvency statement must be made available for inspection by members of the company throughout that meeting" (a bare "must" not done: fork F-must)

-- src:8558 | (4) The validity of a resolution is not affected by a failure to comply with subsection (2) or (3).
@ref s 642(4) Reduction of capital supported by solvency statement: validity (src:8558)
GIVEN `there was a failure to comply with subsection (2) or (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 642(4) the failure affects the validity of the resolution` MEANS
    IF `there was a failure to comply with subsection (2) or (3)`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The validity of a resolution is not affected by a failure to comply with subsection (2) or (3)"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is about "a failure to comply with subsection (2) or (3)"

§§ `s 643 Solvency statement`

-- src:8560 | (1) A solvency statement is a statement that each of the directors—
-- src:8561 | (a) has formed the opinion, as regards the company's situation at the date of the statement, that there is no ground on which the company could then be found to be unable to pay (or otherwise discharge) its debts; and
-- src:8562 | (b) has also formed the opinion—
-- src:8563 | (i) if it is intended to commence the winding up of the company within twelve months of that date, that the company will be able to pay (or otherwise discharge) its debts in full within twelve months of the commencement of the winding up; or
-- src:8564 | (ii) in any other case, that the company will be able to pay (or otherwise discharge) its debts as they fall due during the year immediately following that date.
@ref s 643(1) Solvency statement: what it is (src:8560-8564)
GIVEN `it is intended to commence the winding up of the company within twelve months of the date of the statement` IS A BOOLEAN
      directors IS A LIST OF `s 643(1) director's opinions`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 643(1) the statement is a solvency statement` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF null directors
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a statement "that each of the directors" has formed the opinions says nothing where there is no director to ask
        IF all (GIVEN d YIELD d's `s 643(1)(a) has formed the opinion that there is no ground on which the company could then be found to be unable to pay its debts` AND `the opinion on the winding up or the year` d) directors
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A solvency statement is a statement that each of the directors— (a) has formed the opinion ..., and (b) has also formed the opinion— (i) if it is intended to commence the winding up ... or (ii) in any other case"
    WHERE
        `the opinion on the winding up or the year` d MEANS
            IF `it is intended to commence the winding up of the company within twelve months of the date of the statement`
            THEN d's `s 643(1)(b)(i) has formed the opinion that the company will pay its debts in full within twelve months of the commencement of the winding up`
            ELSE d's `s 643(1)(b)(ii) has formed the opinion that the company will pay its debts as they fall due during the year immediately following the date`

