-- (5): four penalties: on indictment; on summary conviction in England and Wales; in Scotland; in Northern Ireland ("or both" in each).
-- src:8570 | (5) A person guilty of an offence under subsection (4) is liable—
-- src:8571 | (a) on conviction on indictment, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding two years or a fine (or both);
-- src:8572 | (b) on summary conviction—
-- src:8573 | (i) in England and Wales, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding twelve months or to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum (or both);
-- src:8574 | (ii) in Scotland or Northern Ireland, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding six months, or to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum (or both).
@ref s 643(5) Solvency statement: the penalties (src:8570-8574)
GIVEN `the person is guilty of an offence under subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF Penalty)
`s 643(5) the penalty for a person guilty of an offence under subsection (4)` MEANS
    IF `the person is guilty of an offence under subsection (4)`
    THEN JUST (LIST
        (Penalty WITH
            `how convicted` IS `on conviction on indictment`
            `imprisonment not exceeding` IS JUST (Period OF 2, Years)
            `fine not exceeding` IS JUST `a fine without a stated limit`
            `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING
            `imprisonment and fine together` IS TRUE),
        (Penalty WITH
            `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction in England and Wales`
            `imprisonment not exceeding` IS JUST (Period OF 12, Months)
            `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1)
            `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING
            `imprisonment and fine together` IS TRUE),
        (Penalty WITH
            `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction in Scotland`
            `imprisonment not exceeding` IS JUST (Period OF 6, Months)
            `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1)
            `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING
            `imprisonment and fine together` IS TRUE),
        (Penalty WITH
            `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`
            `imprisonment not exceeding` IS JUST (Period OF 6, Months)
            `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1)
            `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING
            `imprisonment and fine together` IS TRUE))
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the liability is that of "A person guilty of an offence under subsection (4)"

