    (Day (`s 644(1) the last day for the documents` `the date the resolution for reducing share capital was passed`)) MINUS (Day `the date the resolution for reducing share capital was passed`)

-- src:8576 | (1) Within 15 days after the resolution for reducing share capital is passed the company must deliver to the registrar—
-- src:8577 | (a) a copy of the solvency statement, and
-- src:8578 | (b) a statement of capital.
-- src:8579 | This is in addition to the copy of the resolution itself that is required to be delivered to the registrar under Chapter 3 of Part 3.
@ref s 644(1) Registration of resolution and supporting documents: in time (src:8576-8579)
GIVEN `the date the resolution for reducing share capital was passed` IS A DATE
      `the date the company delivered the documents to the registrar, if it has` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date being asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 644(1) the company delivered the documents to the registrar in time` MEANS
    `the answer on the dates`
    WHERE
        `the answer on the dates` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the date the company delivered the documents to the registrar, if it has`
            WHEN JUST given THEN
                BRANCH
                    IF given LESS THAN `the date the resolution for reducing share capital was passed`
                    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the period runs "after" the event and a documents given before it is not within the period
                    IF given AT MOST `s 644(1) the last day for the documents` `the date the resolution for reducing share capital was passed`
                    THEN JUST TRUE
                    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Within 15 days after the resolution for reducing share capital is passed the company must deliver to the registrar— (a) a copy of the solvency statement, and (b) a statement of capital"
            WHEN NOTHING THEN
                IF `the date being asked about` GREATER THAN `s 644(1) the last day for the documents` `the date the resolution for reducing share capital was passed`
                THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Within 15 days after the resolution for reducing share capital is passed the company must deliver to the registrar— (a) a copy of the solvency statement, and (b) a statement of capital" (the period of 15 days has ended and nothing was given)
                ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the period of 15 days has not ended, so the text does not yet say whether the duty is met

