        IF `default is made in complying with this section` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If default is made in complying with this section, an offence is committed by"
        IF `s 1121 the officer is in default` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "every officer of the company who is in default" (the officer is not in default, as s 1121 answers)
        IF `default is made in complying with this section` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `s 1121 the officer is in default` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether default is made, or whether the officer is in default (s 1121, coa24), is not known


-- src:8601 | (9) A person guilty of an offence under subsection (7) or (8) is liable—
-- src:8602 | (a) on conviction on indictment, to a fine;
-- src:8603 | (b) on summary conviction, to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum.
@ref s 644(9) Registration of resolution and supporting documents: the penalty (src:8601-8603)
GIVEN `the person is guilty of an offence under subsection (7) or (8)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF Penalty)
`s 644(9) the penalty for a person guilty of an offence under subsection (7) or (8)` MEANS
    IF `the person is guilty of an offence under subsection (7) or (8)`
    THEN JUST (LIST (Penalty WITH
            `how convicted` IS `on conviction on indictment`
            `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
            `fine not exceeding` IS JUST `a fine without a stated limit`
            `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING
            `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE),
                    (Penalty WITH
            `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction`
            `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
            `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1)
            `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING
            `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE))
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person guilty of an offence under subsection (7) or (8) is liable"


§§ `s 645 Application to court for order of confirmation`

-- src:8606 | (1) Where a company has passed a resolution for reducing share capital, it may apply to the court for an order confirming the reduction.
@ref s 645(1) Application to court for order of confirmation (src:8606)
GIVEN `the company has passed a resolution for reducing share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 645(1) the company may apply to the court for an order confirming the reduction` MEANS
    IF `the company has passed a resolution for reducing share capital`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a company has passed a resolution for reducing share capital, it may apply to the court for an order confirming the reduction" ("where": ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))

-- src:8607 | (2) If the proposed reduction of capital involves either—
-- src:8608 | (a) diminution of liability in respect of unpaid share capital, or
-- src:8609 | (b) the payment to a shareholder of any paid-up share capital,
-- src:8610 | section 646 (creditors entitled to object to reduction) applies unless the court directs otherwise.
@ref s 645(2) Application to court for order of confirmation: when section 646 applies (src:8607-8610)
GIVEN `the proposed reduction involves diminution of liability in respect of unpaid share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proposed reduction involves the payment to a shareholder of any paid-up share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court directs otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 645(2) section 646 applies to the reduction, unless the court directs otherwise` MEANS
    IF `the proposed reduction involves diminution of liability in respect of unpaid share capital` OR `the proposed reduction involves the payment to a shareholder of any paid-up share capital`
    THEN IF `the court directs otherwise`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "section 646 (creditors entitled to object to reduction) applies unless the court directs otherwise" (the unless is met: fork F-except-met)
         ELSE JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection is for a reduction that involves "either (a) diminution of liability in respect of unpaid share capital, or (b) the payment to a shareholder of any paid-up share capital"

-- src:8611 | (3) The court may, if having regard to any special circumstances of the case it thinks proper to do so, direct that section 646 is not to apply as regards any class or classes of creditors.
@ref s 645(3) Application to court for order of confirmation: the court may disapply section 646 (src:8611)
GIVEN `the court thinks it proper to do so, having regard to any special circumstances of the case` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 645(3) the court may direct that section 646 is not to apply as regards a class of creditors` MEANS
    IF `the court thinks it proper to do so, having regard to any special circumstances of the case`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The court may, if having regard to any special circumstances of the case it thinks proper to do so, direct that section 646 is not to apply": a power; where the court does not think it proper the text does not say it may not (fork F-645-3, name-test sweep of 2026-11-12)

-- src:8612 | (4) The court may direct that section 646 is to apply in any other case.
@ref s 645(4) Application to court for order of confirmation: the court may apply section 646 in any other case (src:8612)
GIVEN `the case is one other than a case within subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 645(4) the court may direct that section 646 is to apply` MEANS
    IF `the case is one other than a case within subsection (2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the direction is for "any other case"; a case within subsection (2) is already governed by it

-- Section 646(1) says it applies "(see section 645(2) and (4))": the two routes. With neither route taken the answer is NOTHING, not a no: s 645(4) lets the court add cases (fork F-two-routes).
-- src:8607 | (2) If the proposed reduction of capital involves either—
-- src:8608 | (a) diminution of liability in respect of unpaid share capital, or
-- src:8609 | (b) the payment to a shareholder of any paid-up share capital,
-- src:8610 | section 646 (creditors entitled to object to reduction) applies unless the court directs otherwise.
-- src:8611 | (3) The court may, if having regard to any special circumstances of the case it thinks proper to do so, direct that section 646 is not to apply as regards any class or classes of creditors.
-- src:8612 | (4) The court may direct that section 646 is to apply in any other case.
@ref s 645(2) and (4) Application to court for order of confirmation: whether section 646 applies (src:8607-8612)
GIVEN `s 645(2) section 646 applies to the reduction, unless the court directs otherwise` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the court has directed under subsection (4) that section 646 is to apply` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 645 section 646 applies to the reduction` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 645(2) section 646 applies to the reduction, unless the court directs otherwise`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "applies unless the court directs otherwise" (the court has directed otherwise)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        IF `the court has directed under subsection (4) that section 646 is to apply`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "The court may direct that section 646 is to apply in any other case" (s 645(4)); a reduction within neither limb of s 645(2), where the court has given no direction, is a case the court may still bring in, so the text does not say that section 646 does not apply (fork F-two-routes)

§§ `s 646 Creditors entitled to object to reduction`

-- src:8614 | (1) Where this section applies (see section 645(2) and (4)), every creditor of the company who
-- src:8615 | (a) at the date fixed by the court is entitled to any debt or claim that, if that date were the commencement of the winding up of the company would be admissible in proof against the company, and
-- src:8616 | (b) can show that there is a real likelihood that the reduction would result in the company being unable to discharge his debt or claim when it fell due,
-- src:8617 | is entitled to object to the reduction of capital.
@ref s 646(1) Creditors entitled to object to reduction (src:8614-8617)
GIVEN `s 645 section 646 applies to the reduction` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `at the date fixed by the court the creditor is entitled to a debt or claim that would be admissible in proof against the company if that date were the commencement of the winding up` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the creditor can show a real likelihood that the reduction would result in the company being unable to discharge the debt or claim when it fell due` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 646(1) the creditor is entitled to object to the reduction of capital` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 645 section 646 applies to the reduction` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where this section applies (see section 645(2) and (4)), every creditor of the company who ... is entitled to object" (it does not apply)
        IF `s 645 section 646 applies to the reduction` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether section 646 applies is not known
        IF       `at the date fixed by the court the creditor is entitled to a debt or claim that would be admissible in proof against the company if that date were the commencement of the winding up`
             AND `the creditor can show a real likelihood that the reduction would result in the company being unable to discharge the debt or claim when it fell due`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the right is that of "every creditor of the company who (a) ... and (b) ..."; a creditor outside both limbs is not addressed (fork F-who-limbs)

-- src:8618 | (2) The court shall settle a list of creditors entitled to object.
@ref s 646(2) Creditors entitled to object to reduction: the list (src:8618)
GIVEN `s 645 section 646 applies to the reduction` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 646(2) the court is obliged to settle a list of creditors entitled to object` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 645 section 646 applies to the reduction`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where this section applies": the duty is that of the court when section 646 applies (fork F-where-unmet)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether section 646 applies is not known

-- src:8620 | (a) shall ascertain, as far as possible without requiring an application from any creditor, the names of those creditors and the nature and amount of their debts or claims, and
@ref s 646(3)(a) Creditors entitled to object to reduction: the court ascertains the creditors (src:8620)
GIVEN `it is possible to ascertain the creditor's name and the nature and amount of the debt or claim without requiring an application from the creditor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 646(3)(a) the court must ascertain the creditor's name and debt or claim without an application from the creditor` MEANS
    IF `it is possible to ascertain the creditor's name and the nature and amount of the debt or claim without requiring an application from the creditor`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "as far as possible without requiring an application from any creditor"

-- src:8621 | (b) may publish notices fixing a day or days within which creditors not entered on the list are to claim to be so entered or are to be excluded from the right of objecting to the reduction of capital.
@ref s 646(3)(b) Creditors entitled to object to reduction: notices fixing a day (src:8621)
GIVEN `the court has published a notice fixing a day within which creditors not entered on the list are to claim to be entered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the creditor is entered on the list` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the creditor claimed to be entered within the day fixed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 646(3)(b) the creditor is excluded from the right of objecting to the reduction` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the court has published a notice fixing a day within which creditors not entered on the list are to claim to be entered`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the exclusion follows "notices fixing a day or days" that the court "may publish"
        IF `the creditor is entered on the list` OR `the creditor claimed to be entered within the day fixed`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "creditors not entered on the list are to claim to be so entered or are to be excluded from the right of objecting" (the creditor is entered or claimed in time)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:8622 | (4) If a creditor entered on the list whose debt or claim is not discharged or has not determined does not consent to the reduction, the court may, if it thinks fit, dispense with the consent of that creditor on the company securing payment of his debt or claim.
@ref s 646(4) Creditors entitled to object to reduction: dispensing with a creditor's consent (src:8622)
GIVEN `the creditor is entered on the list` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the debt or claim is not discharged or has not determined` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the creditor does not consent to the reduction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company secures payment of the debt or claim` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court thinks fit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 646(4) the court may dispense with the creditor's consent` MEANS
    IF       `the creditor is entered on the list`
         AND `the debt or claim is not discharged or has not determined`
         AND `the creditor does not consent to the reduction`
         AND `the company secures payment of the debt or claim`
         AND `the court thinks fit`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a creditor entered on the list whose debt or claim is not discharged or has not determined does not consent to the reduction, the court may, if it thinks fit, dispense with the consent of that creditor on the company securing payment of his debt or claim"

-- (5): the amount to be appropriated. The two limbs overlap where the company admits the debt and the amount is contingent
-- ("(b) ... or if the amount is contingent or not ascertained"): the text does not choose, so that case is NOTHING (fork F-overlap).
-- src:8623 | (5) For this purpose the debt or claim must be secured by appropriating (as the court may direct) the following amount—
-- src:8624 | (a) if the company admits the full amount of the debt or claim or, though not admitting it, is willing to provide for it, the full amount of the debt or claim;
-- src:8625 | (b) if the company does not admit, and is not willing to provide for, the full amount of the debt or claim, or if the amount is contingent or not ascertained, an amount fixed by the court after the like enquiry and adjudication as if the company were being wound up by the court.
@ref s 646(5) Creditors entitled to object to reduction: the amount to be appropriated (src:8623-8625)
GIVEN `the company admits the full amount of the debt or claim or, though not admitting it, is willing to provide for it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount is contingent or not ascertained` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the full amount of the debt or claim` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount fixed by the court after the like enquiry and adjudication as if the company were being wound up by the court` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 646(5) the amount the debt or claim must be secured by appropriating` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the company admits the full amount of the debt or claim or, though not admitting it, is willing to provide for it` AND `the amount is contingent or not ascertained`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): limb (a) (the company admits or will provide for the full amount) and limb (b) (the amount is contingent or not ascertained) both apply and the text does not choose between them
        IF `the company admits the full amount of the debt or claim or, though not admitting it, is willing to provide for it`
        THEN JUST `the full amount of the debt or claim`
        OTHERWISE `the amount fixed by the court after the like enquiry and adjudication as if the company were being wound up by the court`

§§ `s 647 Offences in connection with list of creditors`

-- src:8627 | (1) If an officer of the company—
-- src:8628 | (a) intentionally or recklessly—
-- src:8629 | (i) conceals the name of a creditor entitled to object to the reduction of capital, or
-- src:8630 | (ii) misrepresents the nature or amount of the debt or claim of a creditor, or
-- src:8631 | (b) is knowingly concerned in any such concealment or misrepresentation,
-- src:8632 | he commits an offence.
@ref s 647(1) Offences in connection with list of creditors (src:8627-8632)
GIVEN `s 1173(1) the holder of the position is an officer of the body corporate` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `intentionally or recklessly conceals the name of a creditor entitled to object to the reduction of capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `intentionally or recklessly misrepresents the nature or amount of the debt or claim of a creditor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is knowingly concerned in any such concealment or misrepresentation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 647(1) the officer commits an offence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 1173(1) the holder of the position is an officer of the body corporate` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If an officer of the company ... he commits an offence" (the person is not an officer, as s 1173(1) answers)
        IF NOT (`intentionally or recklessly conceals the name of a creditor entitled to object to the reduction of capital` OR `intentionally or recklessly misrepresents the nature or amount of the debt or claim of a creditor` OR `is knowingly concerned in any such concealment or misrepresentation`)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If an officer of the company— (a) intentionally or recklessly— (i) conceals ..., or (ii) misrepresents ..., or (b) is knowingly concerned in any such concealment or misrepresentation, he commits an offence"
        IF `s 1173(1) the holder of the position is an officer of the body corporate` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is an officer is s 1173(1) (keel; "includes" a director, manager or secretary)

-- src:8633 | (2) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable—
