                             OR c's `s 648(2)(b) the creditor's debt or claim has been discharged`
                             OR c's `s 648(2)(b) the creditor's debt or claim has determined`
                             OR c's `s 648(2)(b) the creditor's debt or claim has been secured`) creditors
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not confirm the reduction unless it is satisfied, with respect to every creditor ... that either (a) his consent to the reduction has been obtained, or (b) his debt or claim has been discharged, or has determined or has been secured" (the unless is met: fork F-except-met)
    ELSE JUST TRUE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The court must not confirm the reduction unless it is satisfied, with respect to every creditor of the company who is entitled to object to the reduction of capital"

-- src:8641 | (3) Where the court confirms the reduction, it may order the company to publish (as the court directs) the reasons for reduction of capital, or such other information in regard to it as the court thinks expedient with a view to giving proper information to the public, and (if the court thinks fit) the causes that led to the reduction.
@ref s 648(3) Court order confirming reduction: publication (src:8641)
