        IF NOT (`a copy of the court order confirming the reduction has been delivered to the registrar` AND `a statement of capital approved by the court has been delivered to the registrar`)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The registrar, on the delivery of a copy of a court order confirming the reduction ... and of a statement of capital (approved by the court), shall register the order and statement" ("on the delivery": ruling of 2026-11-05 (c))
        IF `s 650(2) the registrar is barred from registering the order` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This is subject to section 650": where section 650 bars registration, or its answer is not known, the duty is not stated

