-- src:8656 | (3) The resolution for reducing share capital, as confirmed by the court's order, takes effect—
-- src:8657 | (a) in the case of a reduction of share capital that forms part of a compromise or arrangement sanctioned by the court under Part 26 (arrangements and reconstructions: general)—
-- src:8658 | (i) on delivery of the order and statement of capital to the registrar, or
-- src:8659 | (ii) if the court so orders, on the registration of the order and statement of capital;
-- src:8660 | (aa) in the case of a reduction of share capital that forms part of a compromise or arrangement sanctioned by the court under Part 26A (arrangements and reconstructions: companies in financial difficulty)—
-- src:8661 | (i) in the case of any company other than one to which sub-paragraph (ii) applies, on delivery of the order and statement of capital to the registrar;
-- src:8662 | (ii) in the case of an overseas company that is not required to register particulars under section 1046, on publication of the order and statement of capital in the Gazette;
-- src:8663 | (iii) in either case, if the court so orders, on the registration of the order and statement of capital;
-- src:8664 | (b) in any case not falling within paragraph (a) or (aa), on the registration of the order and statement of capital.
@ref s 649(3) Registration of order and statement of capital: when the resolution takes effect (src:8656-8664)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 649(3) kind of reduction for the time it takes effect`
      `the court so orders that the resolution takes effect on the registration of the order and statement of capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the order and statement of capital were delivered to the registrar, if they have been` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day the order and statement of capital were registered, if they have been` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day the order and statement of capital were published in the Gazette, if they have been` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 649(3) the day the resolution takes effect` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 649(3)(a) part of a compromise or arrangement sanctioned under Part 26` THEN
        IF `the court so orders that the resolution takes effect on the registration of the order and statement of capital`
        THEN `the day the order and statement of capital were registered, if they have been` -- (a)(ii); NOTHING-kind (silent) until they are
        ELSE `the day the order and statement of capital were delivered to the registrar, if they have been` -- (a)(i); NOTHING-kind (silent) until they are
    WHEN `s 649(3)(aa)(i) part of a compromise or arrangement sanctioned under Part 26A, a company other than an overseas company not required to register particulars under section 1046` THEN
        IF `the court so orders that the resolution takes effect on the registration of the order and statement of capital`
        THEN `the day the order and statement of capital were registered, if they have been` -- (aa)(iii); NOTHING-kind (silent) until they are
        ELSE `the day the order and statement of capital were delivered to the registrar, if they have been` -- (aa)(i); NOTHING-kind (silent) until they are
    WHEN `s 649(3)(aa)(ii) part of a compromise or arrangement sanctioned under Part 26A, an overseas company not required to register particulars under section 1046` THEN
        IF `the court so orders that the resolution takes effect on the registration of the order and statement of capital`
        THEN `the day the order and statement of capital were registered, if they have been` -- (aa)(iii); NOTHING-kind (silent) until they are
        ELSE `the day the order and statement of capital were published in the Gazette, if they have been` -- (aa)(ii); NOTHING-kind (silent) until they are
    WHEN `s 649(3)(b) any case not within paragraph (a) or (aa)` THEN
        `the day the order and statement of capital were registered, if they have been` -- (b); NOTHING-kind (silent) until they are

-- src:8665 | (4) Notice of the registration of the order and statement of capital must be published in such manner as the court may direct.
@ref s 649(4) Registration of order and statement of capital: publishing notice (src:8665)
GIVEN `notice of the registration was published in the manner the court directed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 649(4) notice of the registration was published as the court directed` MEANS
    IF `notice of the registration was published in the manner the court directed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Notice of the registration of the order and statement of capital must be published in such manner as the court may direct" (a bare "must" not done; the text does not say who must publish: fork F-who-publishes)

-- src:8666 | (5) The registrar must certify the registration of the order and statement of capital.
@ref s 649(5) Registration of order and statement of capital: the registrar certifies (src:8666)
GIVEN `the order and statement of capital have been registered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 649(5) the registrar is obliged to certify the registration` MEANS
    IF `the order and statement of capital have been registered`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is to certify "the registration of the order and statement of capital": with none there is nothing to certify (fork F-where-unmet)

-- src:8667 | (6) The certificate—
-- src:8668 | (a) must be signed by the registrar or authenticated by the registrar's official seal, and
@ref s 649(6)(a) Registration of order and statement of capital: signed or sealed (src:8667-8668)
GIVEN `the certificate is signed by the registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1062 the document bears the registrar's official seal` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 649(6)(a) the certificate is signed or authenticated as the section requires` MEANS
    IF `the certificate is signed by the registrar`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 1062 the document bears the registrar's official seal`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The certificate— (a) must be signed by the registrar or authenticated by the registrar's official seal" (a bare "must" not done: fork F-must)
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the document bears the official seal is s 1062 (coa23)

-- src:8669 | (b) is conclusive evidence—
-- src:8670 | (i) that the requirements of this Act with respect to the reduction of share capital have been complied with, and
-- src:8671 | (ii) that the company's share capital is as stated in the statement of capital.
@ref s 649(6)(b) Registration of order and statement of capital: conclusive evidence (src:8669-8671)
GIVEN `a certificate has been given under subsection (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      matter IS A `s 649(6)(b) matter the certificate is evidence of`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 649(6)(b) the certificate is conclusive evidence of the matter` MEANS
    IF NOT `a certificate has been given under subsection (5)`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The certificate" is the one the registrar certifies under subsection (5)
    ELSE CONSIDER matter
         WHEN `s 649(6)(b)(i) the requirements of this Act with respect to the reduction of share capital have been complied with` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 649(6)(b)(ii) the company's share capital is as stated in the statement of capital` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 649(6)(b) some other matter` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the certificate is conclusive evidence of the two matters named

§§ `s 650 Public company reducing capital below authorised minimum`

-- src:8674 | (1) This section applies where the court makes an order confirming a reduction of a public company's capital that has the effect of bringing the nominal value of its allotted share capital below the authorised minimum.
@ref s 650(1) Public company reducing capital below authorised minimum: when it applies (src:8674)
GIVEN `s 4(2) the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court makes an order confirming a reduction of the company's capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the nominal value of the company's allotted share capital after the reduction` IS A NUMBER
      `s 763 the authorised minimum` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 650(1) section 650 applies` MEANS
    IF       `s 4(2) the company is a public company`
         AND `the court makes an order confirming a reduction of the company's capital`
         AND `the nominal value of the company's allotted share capital after the reduction` LESS THAN `s 763 the authorised minimum`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where the court makes an order confirming a reduction of a public company's capital that has the effect of bringing the nominal value of its allotted share capital below the authorised minimum" ("where": ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))

-- src:8675 | (2) The registrar must not register the order unless either—
-- src:8676 | (a) the court so directs, or
-- src:8677 | (b) the company is first re-registered as a private company.
@ref s 650(2) Public company reducing capital below authorised minimum: the registrar (src:8675-8677)
GIVEN `s 650(1) section 650 applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the court so directs` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is first re-registered as a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 650(2) the registrar is barred from registering the order` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 650(1) section 650 applies`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where the court makes an order confirming a reduction of a public company's capital that has the effect of bringing the nominal value of its allotted share capital below the authorised minimum"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether section 650 applies is not known
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the court so directs` OR `the company is first re-registered as a private company`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The registrar must not register the order unless either— (a) the court so directs, or (b) the company is first re-registered as a private company" (the unless is met: fork F-except-met)
        ELSE JUST TRUE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The registrar must not register the order unless either— (a) the court so directs, or (b) the company is first re-registered as a private company"

-- src:8678 | (3) Section 651 provides an expedited procedure for re-registration in these circumstances.
@ref s 650(3) Public company reducing capital below authorised minimum: section 651 (src:8678)
GIVEN `s 650(1) section 650 applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 650(3) section 651 provides an expedited procedure for re-registration` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 650(1) section 650 applies`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in these circumstances"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether section 650 applies is not known

§§ `s 651 Expedited procedure for re-registration as a private company`

-- src:8680 | (1) The court may authorise the company to be re-registered as a private company without its having passed the special resolution required by section 97.
@ref s 651(1) Expedited procedure for re-registration as a private company: the court's power (src:8680)
