    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): s 650(3) offers the procedure "in these circumstances"; section 651(1) states no condition of its own
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether section 650 applies is not known

-- src:8681 | (2) If it does so, the court must specify in the order the changes to the company's name and articles to be made in connection with the re-registration.
@ref s 651(2) Expedited procedure for re-registration as a private company: the order (src:8681)
GIVEN `the order specifies the changes to the company's name` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order specifies the changes to the company's articles` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
