    IF `the order specifies the changes to the company's name` AND `the order specifies the changes to the company's articles`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the court must specify in the order the changes to the company's name and articles to be made in connection with the re-registration" (a bare "must" not done: fork F-must)

-- src:8682 | (3) The company may then be re-registered as a private company if an application to that effect is delivered to the registrar together with—
