    IF       `the court has authorised the re-registration`
         AND `an application to that effect is delivered to the registrar`
         AND `it is delivered with a copy of the court's order`
         AND `it is delivered with notice of the company's name and a copy of the company's articles as altered by the court's order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The company may then be re-registered as a private company if an application to that effect is delivered to the registrar together with— (a) a copy of the court's order, and (b) notice of the company's name, and a copy of the company's articles, as altered by the court's order"

-- src:8685 | (4) On receipt of such an application the registrar must issue a certificate of incorporation altered to meet the circumstances of the case.
@ref s 651(4) Expedited procedure for re-registration as a private company: the certificate (src:8685)
GIVEN `the registrar has received such an application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 651(4) the registrar is obliged to issue a certificate of incorporation altered to meet the circumstances` MEANS
