`s 651(5) the certificate states what the section requires` MEANS
    IF `the certificate states that it is issued on re-registration` AND `the certificate states the date on which it is issued`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The certificate must state that it is issued on re-registration and the date on which it is issued" (a bare "must" not done: fork F-must)

