§§ `s 652 Liability of members following reduction of capital`

-- src:8693 | (1) Where a company's share capital is reduced a member of the company (past or present) is not liable in respect of any share to any call or contribution exceeding in amount the difference (if any) between—
-- src:8694 | (a) the nominal amount of the share as notified to the registrar in the statement of capital delivered under section 644 , 649, 1028A or 1032A of this Act or paragraph 7 of Schedule 4 to the Small Business, Enterprise and Employment Act 2015, and
-- src:8695 | (b) the amount paid on the share or the reduced amount (if any) which is deemed to have been paid on it, as the case may be.
@ref s 652(1) Liability of members following reduction of capital: the cap (src:8693-8695)
GIVEN `the nominal amount of the share as notified to the registrar in the statement of capital` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount paid on the share or the reduced amount which is deemed to have been paid on it` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 652(1) the most a member can be called on to contribute in respect of the share` MEANS
    IF `the nominal amount of the share as notified to the registrar in the statement of capital` GREATER THAN `the amount paid on the share or the reduced amount which is deemed to have been paid on it`
    THEN `the nominal amount of the share as notified to the registrar in the statement of capital` MINUS `the amount paid on the share or the reduced amount which is deemed to have been paid on it`
    ELSE 0 -- "the difference (if any)": no difference is read as 0

-- src:8693 | (1) Where a company's share capital is reduced a member of the company (past or present) is not liable in respect of any share to any call or contribution exceeding in amount the difference (if any) between—
-- src:8694 | (a) the nominal amount of the share as notified to the registrar in the statement of capital delivered under section 644 , 649, 1028A or 1032A of this Act or paragraph 7 of Schedule 4 to the Small Business, Enterprise and Employment Act 2015, and
-- src:8695 | (b) the amount paid on the share or the reduced amount (if any) which is deemed to have been paid on it, as the case may be.
-- src:8696 | (2) This is subject to section 653 (liability to creditor in case of omission from list).
@ref s 652(1) Liability of members following reduction of capital: the member's liability (src:8693-8696)
GIVEN `the amount of the call or contribution` IS A NUMBER
      `the nominal amount of the share as notified to the registrar in the statement of capital` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount paid on the share or the reduced amount which is deemed to have been paid on it` IS A NUMBER
      `the call or contribution is for the debt or claim of a creditor omitted from the list (section 653)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 652(1) the member is liable to the call or contribution` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the amount of the call or contribution` AT MOST `s 652(1) the most a member can be called on to contribute in respect of the share` `the nominal amount of the share as notified to the registrar in the statement of capital` `the amount paid on the share or the reduced amount which is deemed to have been paid on it`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection says only what a member is "not liable" to; it does not say a member is liable to a call within the limit
        IF `the call or contribution is for the debt or claim of a creditor omitted from the list (section 653)`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This is subject to section 653"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a member of the company (past or present) is not liable in respect of any share to any call or contribution exceeding in amount the difference (if any) between (a) the nominal amount of the share as notified to the registrar ... and (b) the amount paid on the share or the reduced amount (if any) which is deemed to have been paid on it"

-- src:8697 | (3) Nothing in this section affects the rights of the contributories among themselves.
@ref s 652(3) Liability of members following reduction of capital: contributories (src:8697)
GIVEN `it is a matter of the rights of the contributories among themselves` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 652(3) this section affects the rights of the contributories among themselves` MEANS
    IF `it is a matter of the rights of the contributories among themselves`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this section affects the rights of the contributories among themselves"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the saving names only the rights of the contributories among themselves

§§ `s 653 Liability to creditor in case of omission from list of creditors`

-- src:8709 | (4) The reference in subsection (1)(b) to a company being unable to pay the amount of a debt or claim has the same meaning as in section 123 of the Insolvency Act 1986 (c. 45) or Article 103 of the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989 (S.I. 1989/2405 (N.I. 19)).
@ref s 653(4) Liability to creditor in case of omission from list of creditors: "unable to pay" (src:8709)
GIVEN `s 123 of the Insolvency Act 1986 or Article 103 of the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989: the company is unable to pay the amount of the debt or claim` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 653(4) after the reduction the company is unable to pay the amount of his debt or claim` MEANS
    `s 123 of the Insolvency Act 1986 or Article 103 of the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989: the company is unable to pay the amount of the debt or claim` -- the meaning is the other Act's (outside the sources): JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING as the caller supplies it

-- src:8699 | (1) This section applies where, in the case of a reduction of capital confirmed by the court—
-- src:8700 | (a) a creditor entitled to object to the reduction of share capital is by reason of his ignorance—
-- src:8701 | (i) of the proceedings for reduction of share capital, or
-- src:8702 | (ii) of their nature and effect with respect to his debt or claim,
-- src:8703 | not entered on the list of creditors, and
-- src:8704 | (b) after the reduction of capital the company is unable to pay the amount of his debt or claim.
@ref s 653(1) Liability to creditor in case of omission from list of creditors: when it applies (src:8699-8704)
GIVEN `the reduction of capital was confirmed by the court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a creditor entitled to object to the reduction of share capital is not entered on the list of creditors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that is by reason of his ignorance of the proceedings for reduction of share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that is by reason of his ignorance of their nature and effect with respect to his debt or claim` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 653(4) after the reduction the company is unable to pay the amount of his debt or claim` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 653(1) section 653 applies` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (   `the reduction of capital was confirmed by the court`
                AND `a creditor entitled to object to the reduction of share capital is not entered on the list of creditors`
                AND (`that is by reason of his ignorance of the proceedings for reduction of share capital` OR `that is by reason of his ignorance of their nature and effect with respect to his debt or claim`))
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where, in the case of a reduction of capital confirmed by the court— (a) a creditor entitled to object ... is by reason of his ignorance ... not entered on the list of creditors, and (b) ..." ("where": ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))
        IF `s 653(4) after the reduction the company is unable to pay the amount of his debt or claim` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) after the reduction of capital the company is unable to pay the amount of his debt or claim"
        IF `s 653(4) after the reduction the company is unable to pay the amount of his debt or claim` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the company is unable to pay is s 123 of the Insolvency Act 1986 or Article 103 of the 1989 Order

-- src:8705 | (2) Every person who was a member of the company at the date on which the resolution for reducing capital took effect under section 649(3) is liable to contribute for the payment of the debt or claim an amount not exceeding that which he would have been liable to contribute if the company had commenced to be wound up on the day before that date.
@ref s 653(2) Liability to creditor in case of omission from list of creditors: the members liable (src:8705)
GIVEN `s 653(1) section 653 applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person was a member of the company at the date on which the resolution for reducing capital took effect under section 649(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 653(2) the person is liable to contribute for the payment of the debt or claim` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 653(1) section 653 applies`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where, in the case of a reduction of capital confirmed by the court"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether section 653 applies is not known
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the person was a member of the company at the date on which the resolution for reducing capital took effect under section 649(3)`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the liability is that of "Every person who was a member of the company at the date on which the resolution for reducing capital took effect"

-- src:8705 | (2) Every person who was a member of the company at the date on which the resolution for reducing capital took effect under section 649(3) is liable to contribute for the payment of the debt or claim an amount not exceeding that which he would have been liable to contribute if the company had commenced to be wound up on the day before that date.
@ref s 653(2) Liability to creditor in case of omission from list of creditors: the most (src:8705)
GIVEN `s 653(2) the person is liable to contribute for the payment of the debt or claim` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the amount the person would have been liable to contribute if the company had commenced to be wound up on the day before that date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 653(2) the most the person is liable to contribute` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 653(2) the person is liable to contribute for the payment of the debt or claim`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST `the amount the person would have been liable to contribute if the company had commenced to be wound up on the day before that date`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the cap is on "an amount not exceeding that which he would have been liable to contribute" under this subsection
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is liable is not known

-- src:8706 | (3) If the company is wound up, the court on the application of the creditor in question, and proof of ignorance as mentioned in subsection (1)(a), may if it thinks fit—
-- src:8707 | (a) settle accordingly a list of persons liable to contribute under this section, and
-- src:8708 | (b) make and enforce calls and orders on them as if they were ordinary contributories in a winding up.
@ref s 653(3) Liability to creditor in case of omission from list of creditors: the court (src:8706-8708)
GIVEN `the company is wound up` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the creditor in question applies to the court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `ignorance as mentioned in subsection (1)(a) is proved` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court thinks fit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 653(3) the court may settle a list of persons liable to contribute and make and enforce calls` MEANS
    IF `the company is wound up` AND `the creditor in question applies to the court` AND `ignorance as mentioned in subsection (1)(a) is proved` AND `the court thinks fit`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the company is wound up, the court on the application of the creditor in question, and proof of ignorance as mentioned in subsection (1)(a), may if it thinks fit (a) settle accordingly a list of persons liable to contribute under this section, and (b) make and enforce calls and orders on them"
